post_install() {
  cat <<'MSG'
openconnect needs a layer-3 TUN driver: Wintun (preferred) or TAP-Windows6.
It loads wintun.dll from the directory of the program, then from the
directory of libopenconnect, then from System32.

  * Windows 10/11: use the WireGuard-signed wintun.dll from
    https://www.wintun.net/ (place it next to openconnect.exe or in System32).
  * ReactOS, or Windows in test-signing mode: the optional mingw-w64-wintun
    package installs a source-built, unsigned wintun.dll into the same bin
    directory as openconnect.exe.

Creating an adapter needs Administrator rights. Without a TUN driver,
openconnect can still run with --script-tun / -S (userspace, e.g. ocproxy).
MSG
}
